  "summary": "Nmap before 7.992 contains a use-after-free vulnerability in DNS::ResolverImpl::process_request in…",
  "details": "Nmap before 7.992 contains a use-after-free vulnerability in DNS::ResolverImpl::process_request in libnetutil/massdns.cc that frees still-referenced requests when rescheduling after DNS server disconnects. Attackers answering for at least two configured DNS servers can force a disconnect and send a precisely timed response to crash the scan, possibly enabling code execution.",
